<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Inclusion&nbsp;of&nbsp;Existing&nbsp;Articles</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I'll definitely keep that in mind. I'm generally hesitant to make up a tale surrounding a non-existent anomaly, because that, to me, just begs the question of &quot;what it is and why doesn't it exist as an article&quot; sort of deal. But, to be honest, it was mostly that dealing with the rosebush from just a standard viewpoint was what inspired this idea in the first place, and so I just kept searching out other, pre-existing articles to use as further examples. I do agree that I can make more directed points if I engineer the anomalies around <em>this</em> story, rather than doing the opposite.</p>
<p>Also, nice example; I just read that tale in the last few days, and it didn't even sink in as relevant to what I'm proposing here.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Much obliged!!</p>

