			<div class="content" id="post-content-4824981">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes<br />
Page Type: SCP Article<br />
Page Layout: Class, containment procedures, how it was found, tests run on it.<br />
Elevator Pitch: Easy way to put it is the SCP looks like an average old man except he is always facing the corner of a room facing magnetic north at midnight and every two hours moves to another corner. His face is always in shadow nothing can be done to see it or probe it. He must always be kept in a perfectly square room made of concrete with an aggregate of bone and seashell one of the few objects he cannot destroy. The walls must be perfectly smooth any cracks or chips in the wall causes the SCP to react and turn the room back to a perfect square. The SCP does this by creating a black shadow around itself that engulfs the room no light can enter this shadow and any who enter are turned to bone and blood. Once the shadow vanishes the room is perfectly square once again though slightly bigger.<br />
Central Narrative: The initial discovery of the SCP in Canada comes first along with a new mobile task force called the Canada goose. The next is an incident involving a chip in the wall and the SCP’s reaction then two files hidden by 05 council. Then a new test which gives a hint to removed files and finally placing the SCP in a perfectly round room. Followed by a major incident report that explains what happened in the missing reports.<br />
Hook/Attention-Grabber: There is more to the SCP than what we see it is hinted he knows foundation secrets. How he kills and changes his room size is unknown as nobody who entered his holding cell during an event has lived and no residue, but bone and blood can be found. There is also the mystery about what this SCP knows and why it scares the higher-ups in the foundation.<br />
Additional Notes: I got into SCP a few months ago and I really wanted to write my own and hope people come to enjoy it.</p>

