					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctordeedeedee" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6573779); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6573779&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606010965" alt="DoctorDeeDeeDee" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6573779)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctordeedeedee" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6573779); return false;" >DoctorDeeDeeDee</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606009274 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Nov 2020 01:41</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13870171/seeking-greenlights:my-eyes-are-up-here">Seeking Greenlights: My Eyes are Up Here</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4824980">
									

<p>Sorry for any misinterpretation I may have caused! I chalk this partially up to my not knowing how much information I should be putting into these posts, lest it come across as too long, causing no one to read it.</p>
<p>Thank you for giving me the opportunity to clarify my stance, which I will do now: This is 100% NOT supposed to be a &quot;haha boob&quot; joke. I now understand how my juxtaposition of the word &quot;comedy&quot; with this piece (which is, indeed, intended to be an anti-harassment tale) caused confusion; the part that I viewed as humorous was the fate of the lecher who, as a result of his inability to quit ogling, was ultimately forced to do so.</p>
<p>A detail I omitted from my brief description that perhaps would have helped me better express my true intentions, one which I do plan to include in the finished piece, should I write it, is that during experimentation, the carved possessive word which seemingly appears on her body is observed to come from no one and nowhere but the SCP itself (i.e. there is no &quot;other being&quot; out there causing it): it is an act of self-claiming, of saying &quot;Lay off; this isn't yours to stare at&quot;.</p>
<p>Speaking of testing, almost all of the test data and containment procedure will, of course, be conducted with Dr. Lopez's full consent and within her comfort bounds. While the SCP is identified as its own separate entity, there is still the sense of it being her body, allowing her primary jurisdiction over it (there's a reason I made the &quot;host&quot; an SCP researcher, meaning that she can be in control of and report most of the data herself).</p>
<p>I acknowledge and agree with your aside - I had failed to take the publication date into reference - and to answer the hypothetical question at the end, yes, I think I am capable of composing this piece in a way that it does not come off as a joke about the female anatomy, but rather as a respectful commentary on harassment with a twist of sweet vengeance towards misogynists. I will be sure to be careful with my wording and have several people check over it prior to anywhere near potential publication.</p>
<p>With all that in mind, I would be absolutely thrilled if you could read through this again with this new context and provide further commentary! If not, I have already taken up plenty of your time discussing these matters. Thank you yet again for talking this through with me!!</p>

							</div>

								
					
