<p>I think there could really be something here. The balance between finances and ethical dilemma is something that I think could easily serve to dramatize very real problems that are going on in the world today, especially if you are the kind of person that keeps up with that kind of thing. There's a space to play in that this creates for a whole range of possibilities.</p>
<p>I will say that I'm hesitant towards the inclusion of existing articles. Not to say that they don't belong in the space (they by all means do), but I think making up scenarios of your own could allow for more flexibility in forming the kind of impact you intend for the article. The <a href="/containment-psychiatry-orientation">Containment Psychiatry Orientation</a> does that towards the end to great effectiveness, using a globally known creature, the vampire, as an example to punctuate a unique kind of cruelty.</p>
<p>All in all, I feel some real gold in this. Consider this a <strong><span style="color: green">greenlight</span></strong>.</p>

